; Leg KB -- HW_TEST_16aq, upstream edit 18 (the bulk-read arm in ttinl()).
;
; ARM A: the Victor runs "CKBULK --nobulk --nodisplay".  Bulk arm OFF -- the control.
;
; READ "v9k: bulk sel= n=" IN STEPKB.OUT BEFORE THE CLOCK.  Decision rule 1:
; a leg whose sel/n disagrees with what the .BAT asked for is VOID, not a null
; result.  This arm must show sel=0 and n = 0.  The reason the counter exists at all is
; that an equivalence test CANNOT see a switch that silently failed -- a
; correct arm returns the byte loop's answer either way -- so "the numbers
; came out the same" is exactly what a broken control looks like.
;
; ALSO RECORD MEAN RUN LENGTH = rxbytes / (bulk n).  That is the mechanism
; variable, not decoration.  Under MAME at 9600 it was 11.9 bytes, because
; rxpeak was 303 of 4,096 and myfillbuf() kept handing back tiny chunks; at
; 38400 rxpeak sits near 2,581 and a refill should return hundreds.  If the
; run length here is not much larger than 11.9, the arm cannot be doing much
; and the result is explained before anyone argues about it.
;
; THIS IS THE CONTROL FOR KA, and it is the same binary in the same places:
; --nobulk turns the arm off at RUN TIME, so there is no code-size
; difference for SS16w's layout sensitivity to act on.  SS16af had to spend
; a whole null leg establishing that; this sheet does not.
;
; THE COMPARISON IS ONLY VALID IF THE ARMS ARE PROTOCOL-IDENTICAL: rxbytes
; equal, same packet count, same retransmissions.  A leg that retransmits
; differently is not comparable and is re-run, not adjusted (SS16ag leg AM).
; If it goes off-shape anyway, compare NON-LINE COST -- host clock minus
; (wire bytes x 260 us) -- which is what made SS16al leg GP usable.
;
; The binary is CKBULK.EXE, 226,330 bytes, md5 a9fa6b5c...  NOT CKERMITW.EXE,
; which is still the 225,822-byte pre-edit build and would answer "Extended
; options not configured" -- the same string the unknown-option control is
; supposed to produce.

set speed 38400
set receive timeout 20
set parity none
set prefixing cautious
set block 3
log packets s16aqKB.pkt
send rcvkb.dat
statistics
